      "id": "https://www.npr.org/2026/10/06/nx-s1-5991854/wildfire-smoke-ecology-birds-wildlife-health",
      "url": "https://www.npr.org/2026/10/06/nx-s1-5991854/wildfire-smoke-ecology-birds-wildlife-health",
      "title": "[NPR Health News] Wildfire smoke affects animals in unique ways. Scientists are trying to understand it",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5712x3213+0+536/resize/1400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2F8d%2F0ebd98c943b98fec6b5e73aca53d%2Fximg-6316.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🪶 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2026%2F10%2F06%2Fnx-s1-5991854%2Fwildfire-smoke-ecology-birds-wildlife-health\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\nThe new field of \"smoke ecology\" examines how wildfire smoke perturbs wild places and animals — and what might be done to prevent its worst mayhem.",
      "date_published": "2026-10-06T09:00:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "NPR Health News",
          "url": "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/"
