      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.resilience.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/07/Partys-Over-res-cover.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🌲 🔭 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.resilience.org%2Fstories%2F2026-10-05%2Foil-war-and-the-fate-of-industrial-societies%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\nThe world teeters on the brink of economic disaster due to energy shortages caused by war. Key oil-producing nations are unable and unwilling to increase output, though prices are high. The solutions being proposed—renewable energy technologies—are coming on line, but not fast enough. Sound familiar?",
